  "id": "COMPOUND:26367 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between CID 127037596 and the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, mediated through multiple targets. The CID 127037596 is implicated in the activity of CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of two distinct compounds: (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. Both of these compounds are linked to the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, indicating a possible mechanism of action involving this transporter. Additionally, CID 127037596 is also associated with TE-6, which is a target of another compound that also interacts with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This suggests that the CID 127037596 may influence the activity of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through different molecular pathways, potentially involving enzyme inhibition or other regulatory mechanisms. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
